stability issues for this radiator. All constraints (allowed options, thickness, and size) are met.\",\"requirements\":[{\"requirement\":\"The radiator must be one of the three candidates listed in candidate_specs.md.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Radiator-R2 is one of the listed candidates.\"},{\"requirement\":\"The radiator must keep its performance over the experiment's lifetime.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"No documentation or meeting notes indicate durability or lifetime concerns for Radiator-R2. The vessel is flushed with dry nitrogen, favoring stable operation.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Radiator thickness between 1 and 6 cm.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Selected thickness is 3 cm, within the allowed range.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Achieve the best possible pion/kaon separation at 10 GeV/c.\",\"status\":\"met\",\"evidence\":\"Radiator-R2 at 3 cm delivers the best simulated pion/kaon separation at 10 GeV/c (4.47 sigma), outperforming all other candidates and thicknesses.\"}]}", "call_id": "call_KFq3Y5231wbN5mDJkSAJX57P", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_089a22be6531fce4006afcf7e40ce487d0a22415e07e7b58ec", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
